{"raw": {"https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Biology_JR10015507": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Science Education/Biology", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-15\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor in Science Education/Biology Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Biology (https:/ /www.uwlax.edu/academics/department/biology/) at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 8/23/2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in Science Education, Biology. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students bene\ufb01t from state- of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. \u00a0 This position is a\ufb03liated with the School of Education (SOE), a leader in innovative, high-quality programs led by dedicated faculty and staff. As a fully accredited School, we partner with local, regional and global educators to provider teacher candidates with rich, hands- on learning experiences that prepare them for exemplary professional practice. We are committed to cultivating a welcoming and respectful environment where all students, faculty, and staff can thrive. Our programs emphasize inclusive teaching practices that support the success of every learner and foster a strong sense of belonging across our campus community. \u00a0The review of applications starts on\u00a0 November 2, 2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 November 2nd \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Biology Required Qualifications: Doctorate in Science Education, Biology discipline or related \ufb01eld. The degree must be earned by the end of the \ufb01rst academic year. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Currently holds or previously held a license in secondary science education in one or more of the following areas: biology, physics, chemistry, or earth science. Minimum of three years of teaching experience in secondary science education in one or more of the following areas: biology, physics, chemistry, or earth science. This experience should have been obtained in U.S. PK\u201312 schools or an equivalent setting. Evidence of commitment to success for all students How to Apply: Required Application Materials: Submit as a \u00a0single \u00a0PDF file:\u00a0 1.\u00a0 Cover letter addressing the required and preferred qualifications 2.\u00a0\u00a0CV or resume 3.\u00a0\u00a0A statement of teaching philosophy 4.\u00a0\u00a0Reference\u00a0 contact information (minimum of 3). Contact Information: Alder Yu ayu@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Teaching-Professor---Exercise-Sports-Science_JR10014672": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Exercise Sports Science", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Teaching Professor - Exercise Sports Science Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Teaching Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Exercise & Sport Science at the University of Wisconsin-La Crosse is searching for a passionate educator with expertise in general exercise science as well as clinical exercise physiology to join our team. We are seeking a full-time, Instructional Academic Staff position that will begin in the August 23, 2027 (the possibility for a January 2027 hire does exist). This is a 9-month position, but comes with summer responsibilities and additional compensation for the summer work. The position requires expertise in clinical exercise physiology and clinical education of graduate students. Additional background in exercise science laboratories is desirable. This individual will also serve as Executive Director of the La Crosse Exercise and Health Program (LEHP), providing management and leadership to a community program developed for the clinical education of students. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students bene\ufb01t from state-of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. The review of applications starts on\u00a0 November 16, 2026 .\u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 November 16th \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Develops and designs curriculum and instructional material relevant to a course of instruction Contributes to the development of teaching and learning scholarly work including publications and presentations Contributes to the strategic development of curriculum and academic content through various mediums to ensure the integrity of the educational mission of the work unit Advises students on academic and career direction within a specific field of study Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction, including assessment of student performance May supervise student employees involved in development or delivery of instruction Collaborates with department faculty and staff to develop teaching strategies relevant to the discipline Department: Exercise Sports Science Required Qualifications: Master's Degree in Clinical Exercise Physiology or closely related field. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Current Advanced Cardiac Life Support (ACLS) certification (if not current, candidates will be\u00a0expected to recertify or get certified their first year). Current American College of Sports Medicine (ACSM) Clinical Exercise Physiologist (CEP) certification (if not current, candidates will be expected to recertify or get certified their first year). At least three years of work experience in applied, clinical, and/or cardiac rehabilitation setting. Evidence of the ability to teach courses at the university level in kinesiology / exercise science.\u00a0 How to Apply: Required Application materials: Cover letter (that addresses the required and preferred quali\ufb01cations) CV/Resume References with contact information (minimum of 3) Contact Information: Brian Udermann budermann@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Data-Science_JR10015740": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Data Science", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor - Data Science Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Mathematics & Statistics at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 8/23/2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in all areas of data science. Preference will be given to candidates with experience in arti\ufb01cial intelligence and machine learning, deep learning, natural language processing, and/or data mining. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students bene\ufb01t from state- of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. \u00a0The review of applications starts on November 6, 2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 November 6th \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Mathematics and Statistics Required Qualifications: Doctorate in\u00a0Data Science, Computer Science, Statistics, Mathematics, Applied Mathematics discipline or related \ufb01eld. The degree must be earned by the end of the \ufb01rst academic year. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Experience of teaching in higher education. Evidence of ability to teach a broad range of courses in data science, statistics, and mathematics. Evidence of ability to sustain on-going research at a teaching university. Evidence of collaborative, interdisciplinary, or applied data science work, with an interest in developing projects that engage faculty from other disciplines and/or industry and community partners. Demonstrated pro\ufb01ciency in programming and data management, evidenced by graduate-level coursework, professional experience, scholarly publications, research projects, teaching experience, or applied use of programming languages such as R, Python, and SQL for data analysis, visualization, or database management. How to Apply: Required Application Materials: Submitted in a single .pdf file: a cover letter (that addresses the required, preferred qualifications, a statement of research plan involving undergraduate students, and a statement of teaching philosophy) CV/Resume References and contact information (minimum of 3) Contact Information: James Peirce jpeirce@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Mathematics---Statistics_JR10015310": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Mathematics & Statistics", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-08\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor - Mathematics & Statistics Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Mathematics & Statistics at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 8/23/2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in all areas of statistics and data science. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students bene\ufb01t from state- of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. \u00a0The review of applications starts on\u00a0 October 26, 2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 October 26th \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Mathematics and Statistics Required Qualifications: Doctorate in\u00a0Statistics discipline or related \ufb01eld. The degree must be earned by the end of the \ufb01rst academic year. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Evidence of ability to teach a broad range of courses in statistics Demonstrated experience or interest in mentoring undergraduate and/or graduate students in scholarly research activities, as evidenced by co-authored presentations, publications, research projects, grant participation; supervision of student research independent studies, theses, or capstone projects; or well-described pathways for future student involvement in research agenda. Demonstrated proficiency in statistical programming and data management, evidenced by graduate-level coursework, professional experience, scholarly publications, research projects, teaching experience, or applied use of programming languages such as R, Python, and SQL for statistical analysis, data visualization, or database management. How to Apply: Required application documents: Cover letter (that addresses the required and preferred quali\ufb01cations) CV/Resume References and their contact information (minimum of 3) Contact Information: Douglas Baumann dbaumann@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Economics-NOTICE-OF-FILING_JR10015684": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Economics NOTICE OF FILING", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nNOTICE OF FILING - Please do not apply to this position as it has been filled. This posting is mandatory to meet a United States Department of Labor requirement. See the job posting for more details. A competitive recruitment and selection process was conducted for this employment opportunity and a U.S. worker was not selected. An application for Alien Employment Certification is being filed on behalf of an alien to fill the employment opportunity. Anyone with documentary evidence relative to the application, or available workers, wages and/or working conditions, may contact the Regional Certifying Office of the Department of Labor at the following address:\u00a0 U.S. Department of Labor Employment and Training Administration Office of Foreign Labor Certification 200 Constitution Avenue NW, Room N\u2013 5311 Washington, DC 20210\u00a0 Institution: University of Wisconsin La Crosse Position Title: Assistant Professor - Economics NOTICE OF FILING Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Business Administration (CBA) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse includes six academic departments and the Small Business Development Center. The CBA has over 3,000 students enrolled in one of the eight majors offered. It also offers seven minors and participates in the UW System\u2019s online MBA consortium. Fully accredited by AACSB International, the CBA is recognized for high-quality faculty, staff, programs, and students, and maintains strong regional and global partnerships. A robust Assurance of Learning program regularly evaluates undergraduate and graduate outcomes, supporting accountability and continuous improvement. The review of applications starts on July 7, 2026. Applications received on or before July 7th are prioritized and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus. Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Economics Required Qualifications: Doctorate in Economics or related field by start date. Expertise in at least one of the following fields: Development Economics, Labor Economics, or Health Economics. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. A demonstrated record of publication in peer-reviewed academic journals in Labor Economics, Health Economics, Development Economics, or closely related areas. Experience teaching courses in one or more of the following areas: data analysis for business, labor economics, health economics, and Women in the U.S. Economy How to Apply: Cover letter (that addresses the required and preferred qualifications) CV / Resume Three to Five references with contact information Contact Information: Sheida Babakhani Teimouri stemouri@uwlax.edu"}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool---SUSTAINABLITY---ENVIROMENTAL-STUDIES_JR10007132": {"title": "Instructor Pool - SUSTAINABILITY & ENVIRONMENTAL STUDIES", "description": "Posted: 2026-10-02\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool - SUSTAINABILITY & ENVIRONMENTAL STUDIES Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u00a0\u00a0The College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21st\u00a0Century global society.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Department: Sustainability & Environmental Studies Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents: Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume Three to five references with contact information\u00a0 Contact Information: Alysa Remsburg aremsburg@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---English_JR10015479": {"title": "Assistant Professor - English", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-30\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor - English Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of English at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for two 9-month tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 8/23/2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in Writing Studies with an emphasis in at least one of the following areas: professional & technical writing, digital content & user experience, and/or emerging writing technologies. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the positions are \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts. The College actively supports the university's General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. As a faculty member in CASSH, you will join colleagues embracing the teacher-scholar model and sharing a deep commitment to student success. Our faculty see teaching and scholarship as connected, with research and creative work enhancing the classroom and mentoring experiences. CASSH prepares students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21st Century global society. \u00a0The review of applications starts on\u00a0 November 2, 2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 November 2nd \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the positions are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: English Required Qualifications: Doctorate in\u00a0Writing Studies or related \ufb01eld. The degree must be earned by the end of the \ufb01rst academic year. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: One term or more experience teaching professional & technical writing One term or more experience teaching in the areas of digital content writing and/or user experience One term or more experience teaching emerging writing technologies One term or more experience teaching grant writing How to Apply: Required application materials Cover letter (that addresses the required and preferred qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume References and their contact information (minimum 3)\u00a0 Contact Information: Lindsay Steiner lsteiner@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Clinical-Assistant-Professor---Health-Professions_JR10015327": {"title": "Clinical Assistant Professor -  Radiation Therapy", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-24\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Clinical Assistant Professor - Radiation Therapy Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Clinical Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Health Professions at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 12-month teaching position at the rank of Clinical Assistant Professor with the start date of 1/7/2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in radiation therapy. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. This is a renewable non-tenure track instructional position. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students bene\ufb01t from state- of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. The review of applications starts on November 2, 2026 \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 November 2nd \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Health Professions Required Qualifications: Bachelor\u2019s degree in Radiation Therapy ARRT-certi\ufb01ed Radiation Therapist A minimum of 4 years clinical experience Required to earn a Master's Degree within 4 years of employment Excellent interpersonal/written communication skills Desire to be a lifelong learner through professional development and networking Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience (clinical experience acceptable) Interest in involvement in Radiation Therapy organizations (ASRT, etc.) Ability to function independently while collaborating effectively with colleagues, peers, and clinical educators Demonstrate leadership, professional behavior, and self-directed learning with minimal supervision to achieve educational and clinical learning objectives How to Apply: Required applications documents Cover letter (that addresses the required and preferred quali\ufb01cations) CV/Resume References and their contact information (minimum of 3) Contact Information: Shauna Salow ssalow@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--MICROBIOLOGY_JR10007194": {"title": "Instructor Pool- MICROBIOLOGY", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- MICROBIOLOGY Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide\u202f state-of-the-art \u202finstructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement.\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Department: Microbiology Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field\u00a0appropriate to\u00a0the needs of the department, or\u00a0significant progress\u00a0toward a doctorate\u00a0degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure,\u00a0or a baccalaureate plus experience,\u00a0can be\u00a0established\u00a0as\u00a0appropriate qualifications\u00a0for the teaching position.\u00a0Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be\u00a0required.\u00a0\u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents:\u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f\u00a0 CV\u202f/ Resume\u00a0 Three to five references with\u00a0contact information\u202f\u00a0 Contact Information: Peter Wilker pwilker@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Special-Collections-Librarian--Assistant-Professor----Murphy-Library_JR10015116": {"title": "Special Collections Librarian (Assistant Professor) - Murphy Library", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-22\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Special Collections Librarian (Assistant Professor) - Murphy Library Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Library Department at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 1/7/2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in Special Collections Librarianship. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, the successful candidate will co-manage\u00a0the Special Collections unit. This includes leading the unit\u2019s collection development activities; managing the unit\u2019s archival appraisal and acquisitions efforts; processing new and backlogged archival materials and collections; cultivating and maintaining donor relations to acquire new materials; overseeing materials that fall under the local classi\ufb01cation for university institutional documents; serving as the point of contact and manager for the library's participation in the Federal and State government document programs; leading efforts to organize, maintain, and promote the library's extensive collection of topographic maps; contributing to unit and departmental information literacy efforts, including Special Collections reference and instruction activities; collaborating with cataloging Special Collections materials in a variety of schemas; and performing conservation activities as necessary. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community, and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or director. As faculty in a student-centered teaching library, Library Department members strive to ensure that UWL students graduate as information literate citizens with the ability to recognize when information is needed, and with the ability to locate, evaluate, and use information effectively and ethically. Department members help provide many services and access to information resources that support and promote excellence in academic study and research, success in teaching and learning, and intellectual and cultural exploration. Murphy Library additionally serves the greater community as a regional information center. \u00a0The review of applications starts on\u00a0 October 22, 2026 .\u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 October 22nd \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Library Department Required Qualifications: Masters in an ALA accredited Library Science program at time of application. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Post-MLS experience working within an academic library setting, specifically involving archives and/or special collections. Experience with the management of records within the archival lifecycle, including appraisal, accession, arrangement and description, collection management, conservation, and access.\u00a0 Experience working with a government documents and/or map collection. Experience in a public-facing role working with students, faculty, community members, and prospective donors. Experience delivering services related to Information Literacy, including both reference and instruction. How to Apply: Required application materials: Cover letter (that addresses the required and preferred quali\ufb01cations) CV/Resume References with their contact information (minimum of 3) Contact Information: David Mindel dmindel@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Public-Health---Community-Health-Education_JR10015061": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Public Health & Community Health Education", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor - Public Health & Community Health Education Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Public Health & Community Health Education at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 8/23/2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in human sexuality and sexual health promotion, grant writing and administration, public health advocacy, health equity and social drivers of health, and the U.S. healthcare system. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students bene\ufb01t from state- of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. \u00a0The review of applications starts on\u00a0 October 14, 2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 October 14th \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Public Health & Community Health Education Required Qualifications: Doctorate in \u00a0 Public Health, Community Health, Health Education/Promotion discipline or related \ufb01eld. The degree must be earned by the end of the \ufb01rst academic year. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated excellence in teaching in higher education Evidence of an active research agenda that can be maintained and developed across campus and in the community Experience with accreditation Demonstrated experience outside of academia in public health or health education and health promotion practice Certi\ufb01ed Health Education Specialist (CHES), Master Certi\ufb01ed Health Education Specialist (MCHES), and/or Certi\ufb01ed in Public Health (CPH) How to Apply: Required application materials: Cover letter (that addresses the required and preferred quali\ufb01cations) CV/Resume References and their contact information (minimum of 3) Contact Information: Sarah Pember spember@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Physical-Education_JR10014839": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Physical Education", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor - Physical Education Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Exercise & Sport Science at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of August 23, 2027 with potential of an early start January 2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in Physical Education, Adapted Physical Education and/or Health Education. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students bene\ufb01t from state- of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. This position is a\ufb03liated with the School of Education (SOE), a leader in innovative, high-quality programs led by dedicated faculty and staff. As a fully accredited School, we partner with local, regional and global educators to provider teacher candidates with rich, hands- on learning experiences that prepare them for exemplary professional practice. We are committed to cultivating a welcoming and respectful environment where all students, faculty, and staff can thrive. Our programs emphasize inclusive teaching practices that support the success of every learner and foster a strong sense of belonging across our campus community. \u00a0The review of applications starts on\u00a0 October 15, 2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 October 15th \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Exercise Sports Science Required Qualifications: Doctorate in Physical Education, Adapted Physical Education, Health Education or a closely related \ufb01eld discipline or related \ufb01eld. The degree must be earned by the end of the \ufb01rst academic year. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Currently holds or previously held a license in physical education, a dapted p hysical e ducation and/or school health education. Minimum of 3 years physical education and/or school health education teaching experience in U.S. PK-12 schools or the equivalent Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrate knowledge of and experience planning, teaching, and assessing standards-based physical education and school health education Demonstrate knowledge of adapted physical education pedagogy Evidence of an emerging research agenda related to physical education, a dapted p hysical e ducation and/or school health education How to Apply: Required application materials: Cover letter (that addresses the required and preferred qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume References and contact information\u00a0(minimum of 3) Contact Information: Sarah Mosley smosley@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Anatomy-Physiology_JR10014928": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Anatomy/Physiology", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor - Anatomy/Physiology Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Exercise & Sport Science at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 8/23/2027 with the potential of starting January 2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in but not limited to: exercise physiology, human physiology, integrative physiology, applied physiology, systemic physiology (cardiorespiratory, metabolic, neurological, etc.), pathophysiology, or related \ufb01elds. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students bene\ufb01t from state- of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. The review of applications starts on\u00a0 October 9, 2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 October 9th \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Exercise Sports Science Required Qualifications: Doctorate in \u00a0 Exercise Physiology/Kinesiology/Exercise Science discipline or related \ufb01eld. The degree must be earned by the end of the \ufb01rst academic year. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated excellence in teaching and research.\u00a0 Evidence of ability to contribute to multiple areas of undergraduate and/or graduate curriculum in the Department of Exercise and Sport Science. How to Apply: Required application materials: Cover letter (that addresses the required and preferred quali\ufb01cations) CV/Resume References and their contact information (minimum of 3) Contact Information: Eileen Narcotta-Welp enarcotta- welp@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Biology-Food-Science_JR10014913": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Biology Food Science", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-11\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor - Biology Food Science Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Biology at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 8/23/2027 or the potential of an early start in January 2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in Food Science. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students bene\ufb01t from state- of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. \u00a0The review of applications starts on\u00a0 October 11, 2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 October 11th \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position is filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Biology Required Qualifications: Doctorate in \u00a0 Food Science discipline or related \ufb01eld. The degree must be earned by the end of the \ufb01rst academic year. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: At least one year of experience teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses in Food and Nutrition Science or related disciplines, with evidence of instructional effectiveness. Evidence of the ability to develop an independent research agenda that engages undergraduate and M.S. students, demonstrated through peer-reviewed publications, grant activity, and/or prior student research mentoring. At least one semester of university-level teaching experience in food science, food safety, or a related field as an instructor of record, co-instructor, or teaching assistant with substantial teaching responsibilities. How to Apply: Required application materials: Submit as a single .pdf file: 1) a cover letter that addresses the required and preferred qualifications, 2) a statement of research plan involving \u00a0 undergraduate students, and 3) a statement of teaching philosophy CV/Resume References and contact information (minimum of 3) Contact Information: Adam Schneider aschneider2@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Anatomy-Physiology_JR10014752": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Exercise Science/Kinesiology", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor - Exercise Science/Kinesiology Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Exercise & Sport Science at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 8/23/2027 with potential of an early start January 2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in Applied Exercise Science & Human Performance including, but not limited to strength and conditioning, exercise programming and \ufb01tness assessment, physical activity promotion, sport analytics and wearable technology, sport and exercise nutrition, adapted and inclusive physical activity, sport and exercise psychology, exercise across the lifespan and aging, or related areas. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students bene\ufb01t from state-of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. \u00a0The review of applications starts on\u00a0 October 14, 2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 October 14th \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Exercise Sports Science Required Qualifications: Doctorate in Exercise science/kinesiology discipline or related \ufb01eld. The degree must be earned by \u00a0 the end of the \ufb01rst academic year. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated excellence in research/scholarship Evidence of successful teaching experience in two or more undergraduate and/or graduate Exercise & Sport Science subject areas, as demonstrated through course instruction, curriculum development, or program leadership. How to Apply: Required application materials: Cover letter (that addresses the required and preferred quali\ufb01cations) CV/Resume References and their contact information (minimum of 3) Contact Information: Teri Hepler thepler@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Analytical-Chemistry_JR10014469": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Analytical Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-08\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor - Analytical Chemistry Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Chemistry & Biochemistry at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 8/23/2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in Analytical Chemistry. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the \ufb01rst review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is \ufb01lled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding o\ufb03ce hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students bene\ufb01t from state-of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. \u00a0The review of applications starts on\u00a0 October 9, 2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 October 9th \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Contributes to the strategic development of curriculum and academic content through various mediums to ensure the integrity of the educational mission of the work unit Contributes to the development of teaching and learning scholarly work including publications and presentations Collaborates with department faculty and staff to develop teaching strategies relevant to the discipline May supervise student employees involved in development or delivery of instruction Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction, including assessment of student performance Advises students on academic and career direction within a specific field of study Develops and designs curriculum and instructional material relevant to a course of instruction Department: Chemistry and Biochemistry Required Qualifications: Doctorate in \u00a0 Chemistry discipline or related \ufb01eld. The degree must be earned by the end of the \ufb01rst academic year. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Prior \u00a0 higher \u00a0 education teaching experience and ability to teach Analytical Chemistry and General Chemistry lecture and \u00a0 laboratory courses \u00a0 A research plan that is \u00a0 appropriate \u00a0 for \u00a0 a Primarily Undergraduate Institution, and that complements the needs of the \u00a0 department A demonstrated record of\u00a0publication in peer-reviewed academic journals \u00a0 Ability to \u00a0 contribute to shared efforts supporting \u00a0 the growth and maintenance of instrumentation resources within the department \u00a0 How to Apply: Required Application Materials: Submit as a single .pdf file: 1) a cover letter that addresses the required and preferred qualifications, 2) a statement of research plan involving \u00a0 undergraduate students, and 3) a statement of teaching philosophy CV/Resume References and contact information (minimum of 3) Contact Information: Kristofer Rolfhus krolfhus@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Physical-Chemistry_JR10014293": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Physical Chemistry", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor - Physical Chemistry Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Chemistry &Biochemistry at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 8/23/2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in experimental physical chemistry. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the first review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university, community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) is the largest academic unit at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse, bringing together diverse disciplines across the natural, physical, computational, and health sciences. Home to 11 academic departments and nationally recognized professional programs, CSH is known for its strong tradition of faculty mentorship, hands-on undergraduate research, and graduate education that prepares students for leadership in science, healthcare, and industry. Faculty and students benefit from state-of-the-art facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which support innovative teaching, collaborative research, and community engagement. The college also hosts interdisciplinary centers and institutes that connect scholarship with real-world challenges, ranging from river studies to disability health. With robust instrumentation, collaborative partnerships -- including ties with the Mayo Clinic Health System -- and potential start-up support, CSH provides new faculty with an environment that fosters both scholarly excellence and student success. \u00a0The review of applications starts on\u00a0 October 9,2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 October 9th \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Chemistry & Biochemistry Required Qualifications: Doctorate in chemistry discipline or related field. The degree must be earned by the end of the first academic year. Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor. Evidence of clear and effective communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: Prior teaching experience and ability to teach General Chemistry and Physical Chemistry lecture and laboratory courses. A research plan in experimental physical chemistry that is appropriate for a Primarily Undergraduate Institution, and that complements the needs of the department. A demonstrated record of, or strong potential for, publication in peer-reviewed academic journals. How to Apply: Required Application Materials: Submitted in a single .pdf file: a cover letter (that addresses the required, preferred qualifications a statement of research plan involving undergraduate students, and a statement of teaching philosophy) CV/Resume References and contact information (minimum of 3) Contact Information: Keith Beyer kbeyer@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Microbiology_JR10014767": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Microbiology", "description": "Posted: 2026-09-04\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal applicati