/www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--ART_JR10007200": {"title": "Instructor Pool- ART", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-24\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- ART Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 \u00a0 The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u202f\u202fThe College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. \u00a0 As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21 st \u202fCentury global society. \u202f\u202f\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Department: Art Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Terry Lilly tlilly@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--ENGLISH_JR10007201": {"title": "Instructor Pool- ENGLISH", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-24\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- ENGLISH Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 \u00a0 The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u202f\u202fThe College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. \u00a0 As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21 st \u202fCentury global society. \u202f\u202f\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Department: English Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Darci Thoune dthoune@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool---STUDENT-AFFAIRS-ADMINISTRATION_JR10007297": {"title": "Instructor Pool - STUDENT AFFAIRS ADMINISTRATION", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-16\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool - STUDENT AFFAIRS ADMINISTRATION Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW. The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u00a0\u00a0The College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21st\u00a0Century global society.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Student Affairs Administration Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume Three to five references with contact information\u00a0 Contact Information: Becki Elkins belkins@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor_JR10012974": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-15\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Professor Job Category: Faculty Employment Type: Regular Job Profile: Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Accountancy at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse is seeking applicants for a 9-month tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor with the start date of 8/23/2027. We encourage applications from candidates with expertise in Accounting. Come join a community of teacher/scholars committed to student success. Applications received prior to the first review date will receive full consideration, and the search will continue on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Under general supervision of the department chair, successful candidates will be responsible forteaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses (if applicable) and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students' work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. The successful candidate is expected to maintain an active, on-going program of scholarship appropriate to their discipline. In addition, faculty provide service to the department, college, university ,community and/or professional organizations. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Business Administration (CBA) at the University of Wisconsin - La Crosse includes six academic departments and the Small Business Development Center. The CBA has over 3,000 students enrolled in one of the eight majors offered. It also offers seven minors and participates in the UW System's online MBA consortium. Fully accredited by the AACSB International, the CBA is recognized for high-quality faculty, staff, programs, and students, and maintains strong regional and global partnerships. A robust Assurance of Learning program regularly evaluates undergraduate and graduate outcomes, supporting accountability and the continuous improvement. \u00a0The review of applications starts on\u00a0 September 9, 2026 . \u00a0Applications received on or before\u00a0 September 9th \u00a0are\u00a0prioritized\u00a0and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually, with shortlisted candidates invited to campus.\u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Department: Accountancy Required Qualifications: PhD or DBA in Accountancy or related field. The degree must be earned by the end of the first academic year.\u00a0 Evidence of the ability to be an effective instructor.\u00a0 Evidence of clear and effective communication skills.\u00a0 Preferred Qualifications: Degree from an AACSB-accredited institution Demonstrated potential for research and publications consistent with AACSB International accreditation standards Certified Public Accountant license from the United States. How to Apply: Cover letter (that addresses the required and preferred qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume Reference and contact information\u00a0for 3-5 references Contact Information: Mehtap Eklund meklund@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructional-Pool---PHILOSOPHY_JR10007135": {"title": "Instructional Pool - PHILOSOPHY", "description": "Posted: 2026-07-13\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructional Pool - PHILOSOPHY Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u00a0\u00a0The College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21st\u00a0Century global society.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Philosophy Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents: Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume Three to five references with contact information\u00a0 Contact Information: Sherri Ross stuttleross@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--MUSIC_JR10007169": {"title": "Instructor Pool- MUSIC", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-27\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- MUSIC Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u202f\u202fThe College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. \u00a0 As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21 st \u202fCentury global society. \u202f\u202f\u202f \u00a0 \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Music Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Jonathan Borja jborja@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--MATHEMATICS-AND-STATISTICS_JR10007147": {"title": "Instructor Pool- MATHEMATICS AND STATISTICS", "description": "Posted: 2026-05-21\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- MATHEMATICS AND STATISTICS Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide\u202f state-of-the-art \u202finstructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement.\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Mathematics and Statistics Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Jennifer Kosiak jkosiak@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--Recreation-Management---Recreational-Therapy_JR10008558": {"title": "Instructor Pool- Recreation Management & Recreational Therapy", "description": "Posted: 2026-02-16\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- Recreation Management & Recreational Therapy Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. \u00a0 Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202f WHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide\u00a0state-of-the-art\u00a0instructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement.\u00a0 \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. \u00a0 If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Recreation Management & Recreational Therapy Required Qualifications: Required: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications) CV\u00a0/ Resume References: 3-5 names and contact information Contact Information: Laurie Harmon lharmon@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool---DANCE_JR10008048": {"title": "Instructor Pool - DANCE", "description": "Posted: 2026-01-29\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool - DANCE Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u00a0\u00a0The College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21st\u00a0Century global society.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department Theatre & Dance Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications) CV/Resume Three - Five References with contact information Contact Information: Laurie Kincman lkincman@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool---THEATRE---DANCE_JR10007122": {"title": "Instructor Pool - THEATRE", "description": "Posted: 2026-01-29\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool - THEATRE Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u00a0\u00a0The College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21st\u00a0Century global society.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department Theatre & Dance Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications) CV/Resume Three - Five References with contact information Contact Information: Laurie Kincman lkincman@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool---Institute-for-Professional-Studies-in-Education--IPSE-_JR10007567": {"title": "Instructor Pool - Institute for Professional Studies in Education (IPSE)", "description": "Posted: 2026-01-13\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool - Institute for Professional Studies in Education (IPSE) Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW. The School of Education (SOE) is a leader in innovative, high-quality programs led by dedicated faculty and staff. As a fully accredited School, we partner with local, regional, and global educators to provide teacher candidates with rich, hands-on learning experiences that prepare them for exemplary professional practice.\u00a0 We are committed to cultivating a welcoming and respectful environment where all students, faculty, and staff can thrive. Our programs emphasize inclusive teaching practices that support the success of every learner and foster\u00a0a strong sense\u00a0of belonging across our campus community.\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: \u00a0Institute for Professional Studies in Education (IPSE) Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents: Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications and indicates to which specific graduate degree or licensure you are applying to teach)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume and a copy of current teaching license Three to five references with contact information\u00a0 Contact Information: Jeannette Armstrong jarmstrong@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--COMMUNICATION-STUDIES_JR10007192-1": {"title": "Instructor Pool- COMMUNICATION STUDIES", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- COMMUNICATION STUDIES Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u202f\u202fThe College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. \u00a0 As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21 st \u202fCentury global society. \u202f\u202f\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Communication Studies Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Kate Lavelle klavelle@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--FINANCE_JR10007197": {"title": "Instructor Pool- FINANCE", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- FINANCE Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 \u00a0 The College of Business Administration (CBA) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse includes six academic departments and the Small Business Development Center. The CBA has over 3,000 students enrolled in one of the eight majors offered. It also offers seven minors and\u202f participates \u202fin the UW System\u2019s online MBA consortium. Fully accredited by AACSB International, the CBA is recognized for high-quality faculty, staff, programs, and students, and\u202f maintains \u202fstrong regional and global partnerships. A robust\u202f Assurance of \u202fLearning program regularly evaluates undergraduate and graduate outcomes, supporting accountability and continuous improvement.\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Finance Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Nilakshi Borah nborah@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--MANAGEMENT_JR10007196-1": {"title": "Instructor Pool- MANAGEMENT", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- MANAGEMENT Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 The College of Business Administration (CBA) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse includes six academic departments and the Small Business Development Center. The CBA has over 3,000 students enrolled in one of the eight majors offered. It also offers seven minors and\u202f participates \u202fin the UW System\u2019s online MBA consortium. Fully accredited by AACSB International, the CBA is recognized for high-quality faculty, staff, programs, and students, and\u202f maintains \u202fstrong regional and global partnerships. A robust\u202f Assurance of \u202fLearning program regularly evaluates undergraduate and graduate outcomes, supporting accountability and continuous improvement.\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Management Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Anup Menon Nandialath anandialath@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--POLITICAL-SCIENCE-AND-PUBLIC-ADMINISTRATION_JR10007204": {"title": "Instructor Pool- POLITICAL SCIENCE AND PUBLIC ADMINISTRATION", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- POLITICAL SCIENCE AND PUBLIC ADMINISTRATION Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 \u00a0 The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u202f\u202fThe College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. \u00a0 As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21 st \u202fCentury global society. \u202f\u202f\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Political Science and Public Administration Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Adam Van Liere avanliere@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--ECONOMICS_JR10007202-1": {"title": "Instructor Pool- ECONOMICS", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- ECONOMICS Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 \u00a0 The College of Business Administration (CBA) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse includes six academic departments and the Small Business Development Center. The CBA has over 3,000 students enrolled in one of the eight majors offered. It also offers seven minors and\u202f participates \u202fin the UW System\u2019s online MBA consortium. Fully accredited by AACSB International, the CBA is recognized for high-quality faculty, staff, programs, and students, and\u202f maintains \u202fstrong regional and global partnerships. A robust\u202f Assurance of \u202fLearning program regularly evaluates undergraduate and graduate outcomes, supporting accountability and continuous improvement.\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Economics Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Sheia Babakhani Teimouri steimouri@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--INFORMATION-SYSTEMS_JR10007206": {"title": "Instructor Pool- INFORMATION SYSTEMS", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- INFORMATION SYSTEMS Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 The College of Business Administration (CBA) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse includes six academic departments and the Small Business Development Center. The CBA has over 3,000 students enrolled in one of the eight majors offered. It also offers seven minors and\u202f participates \u202fin the UW System\u2019s online MBA consortium. Fully accredited by AACSB International, the CBA is recognized for high-quality faculty, staff, programs, and students, and\u202f maintains \u202fstrong regional and global partnerships. A robust\u202f Assurance of \u202fLearning program regularly evaluates undergraduate and graduate outcomes, supporting accountability and continuous improvement.\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Information Systems Required Qualifications: \u00a0 Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Peter Haried pharied@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--PUBLIC-HEALTH-AND-COMMUNITY-HEALTH-EDUCATION_JR10007205": {"title": "Instructor Pool- PUBLIC HEALTH AND COMMUNITY HEALTH EDUCATION", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- PUBLIC HEALTH AND COMMUNITY HEALTH EDUCATION Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 \u00a0 The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide\u202f state-of-the-art \u202finstructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement.\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Public Health and Community Health Education Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Sarah Pember spember@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--RACE--GENDER--AND-SEXUALITY-STUDIES_JR10007137": {"title": "Instructor Pool- RACE, GENDER, AND SEXUALITY STUDIES", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- RACE, GENDER, AND SEXUALITY STUDIES Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW \u00a0 The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u202f\u202fThe College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. \u00a0 As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21 st \u202fCentury global society. \u202f\u202f\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Race, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Terry Lilley tlilley@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool---COMPUTER-SCIENCE---COMPUTER-ENGINERING_JR10007138": {"title": "Instructor Pool - COMPUTER SCIENCE & COMPUTER ENGINERING", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool - COMPUTER SCIENCE & COMPUTER ENGINERING Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide\u00a0state-of-the-art\u00a0instructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement.\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Computer Science & Computer Engineering Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents: Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume Three to five references with contact information\u00a0 Contact Information: Kenny Hunt khunt@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool---PHYSICS_JR10007142": {"title": "Instructor Pool - PHYSICS", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool - PHYSICS Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW. The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide\u00a0state-of-the-art\u00a0instructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement.\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Physics Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents: Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume Three to five references with contact information\u00a0 Contact Information: Jennifer Docktor jdocktor@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool---HISTORY_JR10007129": {"title": "Instructor Pool - HISTORY", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool - HISTORY Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u00a0\u00a0The College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21st\u00a0Century global society.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: History Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents: Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume Three to five references with contact information\u00a0 Contact Information: Victor Macias-Gonzalez vmacias-gonzalez@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--CHEMISTRY-AND-BIOCHEMISTRY_JR10007126": {"title": "Instructor Pool- CHEMISTRY AND BIOCHEMISTRY", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- CHEMISTRY AND BIOCHEMISTRY Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW \u00a0 The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide\u202f state-of-the-art \u202finstructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement.\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Chemistry and Biochemistry Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required Application Documents: Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Todd Weaver tweaver@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool---GEOGRAPHY-AND-ENVIRONMENTAL-SCIENCE_JR10007158": {"title": "Instructor Pool - GEOGRAPHY AND ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool - GEOGRAPHY AND ENVIRONMENTAL SCIENCE Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW. The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide\u00a0state-of-the-art\u00a0instructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement.\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Geography and Environmental Science Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents: Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume Three to five references with contact information\u00a0 Contact Information: Joan Bunbury jbunbury@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--DEPARTMENT-OF-EDUCATIONAL-STUDIES_JR10007154": {"title": "Instructor Pool- DEPARTMENT OF EDUCATIONAL STUDIES", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- DEPARTMENT OF EDUCATIONAL STUDIES Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 The School of Education (SOE) is a leader in innovative, high-quality programs led by dedicated faculty and staff. As a fully accredited School, we partner with local, regional, and global educators to provide teacher candidates with rich, hands-on learning experiences that prepare them for exemplary professional practice.\u202f \u00a0 We are committed to cultivating a welcoming and respectful environment where all students, faculty, and staff can thrive. Our programs emphasize inclusive teaching practices that support the success of every learner and foster\u202f a strong sense \u202fof belonging across our campus community.\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Department of Educational Studies Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Heather Linville hlinville@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool---BIOLOGY_JR10007152-1": {"title": "Instructor Pool - BIOLOGY", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool - BIOLOGY Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW. The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide\u00a0state-of-the-art\u00a0instructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement.\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Biology Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents: Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume Three to five references with contact information\u00a0 Contact Information: Anton Sanderfoot asanderfoot@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--GRADUATE-AND-EXTENDED-LEARNING_JR10006878": {"title": "Instructor Pool- GRADUATE AND EXTENDED LEARNING", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- GRADUATE AND EXTENDED LEARNING Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW Graduate & Extended Learning expands UWL\u2019s role in serving Wisconsin, through our work with youth and with our adult, professional, and continuing education programs. Our office is very collaborative, and our work\u00a0provides\u00a0the chance to interact with a diverse group of individuals. Our partners include colleagues on and off campus, instructors, and students \u2013 ranging from middle schoolers who are just learning what college is all about \u2013 to adults who\u00a0seek\u00a0to move forward in their careers. We play a key role in UWL\u2019s commitment to community engagement and workforce development.\u00a0 \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Graduate and Extended Learning Required Qualifications: Required: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications) CV\u00a0/ Resume References: 3-5 names and contact information Contact Information: Meredith Thomsen mthomsen@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool---GLOBAL-CULTURES-AND-LANGUAGES_JR10007145": {"title": "Instructor Pool - GLOBAL CULTURES AND LANGUAGES", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool - GLOBAL CULTURES AND LANGUAGES Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse maintains an ongoing search to serve as a pool of potential instructors for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of the relevant department chair. The instructor is responsible for teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and holding classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. In addition, workload may involve advising students and/or providing other service to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. POOL\u00a0SEARCHES\u00a0MAY\u00a0NOT\u00a0BE\u00a0CURRENTLY\u00a0ENGAGED\u00a0IN\u00a0ACTIVE\u00a0HIRING.\u00a0WHEN\u00a0POSITIONS\u00a0ARE\u00a0NEEDED,\u00a0DEPARTMENTS\u00a0WILL\u00a0REVIEW\u00a0APPLICATIONS\u00a0AND\u00a0CONTACT\u00a0YOU\u00a0TO\u00a0CONFIRM\u00a0CONTINUED\u00a0INTEREST/SCHEDULE\u00a0AN\u00a0INTERVIEW. The College of Arts, Social Sciences, and Humanities (CASSH) is a vibrant academic community bringing together the strengths of the liberal arts, innovative interdisciplinary programs, and the creative energy of the School of Visual and Performing Arts.\u00a0\u00a0The College actively supports the university\u2019s General Education Program and offers a robust number of undergraduate degrees and three graduate programs. As an instructor in CASSH, you will join colleagues who share a deep commitment to student success as we prepare students for both meaningful careers as well as citizenship in 21st\u00a0Century global society.\u00a0\u00a0\u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and maintain work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions regarding this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Global Cultures and Languages Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field appropriate to the needs of the department, or significant progress toward a doctorate degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure, or a baccalaureate plus experience, can be established as appropriate qualifications for the teaching position. Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be required. How to Apply: Required application documents: Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u00a0 CV\u00a0/ Resume Three to five references with contact information\u00a0 Contact Information: Omar Granados ogranados@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--HEALTH-PROFESSIONS_JR10007141": {"title": "Instructor Pool- HEALTH PROFESSIONS", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- HEALTH PROFESSIONS Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW. The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide\u202f state-of-the-art \u202finstructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement.\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Health Professions Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Thomas Kernozek tkernozek@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Instructor-Pool--EXERCISE-AND-SPORT-SCIENCE_JR10007167": {"title": "Instructor Pool- EXERCISE AND SPORT SCIENCE", "description": "Posted: 2025-12-23\nPart time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Instructor Pool- EXERCISE AND SPORT SCIENCE Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Lecturer Job Duties: Each department at the University of Wisconsin \u2013 La Crosse \u00a0 maintains \u00a0 an ongoing search to \u00a0 serve as a pool of pot ential instructors \u00a0 for program needs. If hired from this pool, the instructor will be under the general supervision of \u00a0 the \u00a0 relevant \u00a0 department \u00a0 chair . \u00a0 The i nstructor \u00a0 is responsible for \u00a0 teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses. In addition to preparing for and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 classes [face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online], teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, \u00a0 providing regular and substantive feedback on student work, \u00a0 maintaining appropriate records, and \u00a0 holding \u00a0 office \u00a0 hours. In addition, \u00a0 workload \u00a0 may involve advising students and/or providing other \u00a0 service \u00a0 to the department. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. \u00a0 \u00a0 POOL\u202fSEARCHES\u202fMAY\u202fNOT\u202fBE\u202fCURRENTLY\u202fENGAGED\u202fIN\u202fACTIVE\u202fHIRING.\u202fWHEN\u202fPOSITIONS\u202fARE\u202fNEEDED,\u202fDEPARTMENTS\u202fWILL\u202fREVIEW\u202fAPPLICATIONS\u202fAND\u202fCONTACT\u202fYOU\u202fTO\u202fCONFIRM\u202fCONTINUED\u202fINTEREST/SCHEDULE\u202fAN\u202fINTERVIEW . \u00a0 The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide\u202f state-of-the-art \u202finstructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement.\u202f \u00a0 UW-La Crosse does not offer H-1B or other work authorization visa sponsorship for this position. Candidates must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and \u00a0 maintain \u00a0 work authorization throughout the employment term. If you have questions \u00a0 regarding \u00a0 this, please contact Human Resources at 608-785-8013. \u00a0 Key Job Responsibilities: Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction for one or more courses, including assessment of student performance Develops instructional design and curriculum relevant to a course of instruction Serves as an initial point of contact for students as it relates to specific course or series content and expectations Department: Exercise and Sport Science Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s Degree in a field \u00a0 appropriate to \u00a0 the needs of the department, or \u00a0 significant progress \u00a0 toward a doctorate \u00a0 degree, or, in rare circumstances, post-baccalaureate certification or licensure , \u00a0 or a baccalaureate plus experience , \u00a0 can be \u00a0 established \u00a0 as \u00a0 appropriate qualifications \u00a0 for the teaching position. \u00a0 Depending on the program, specific certification/licensure or clinical experience may be \u00a0 required . \u00a0 How to Apply: Required application documents: \u00a0 Cover letter (that addresses the required qualifications)\u202f \u00a0 CV\u202f / Resume \u00a0 Three to five r eference s with \u00a0 contact information\u202f \u00a0 Contact Information: Naoko Giblin ngiblin@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 Paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 Excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 Paid holidays and paid sick days. After 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 Benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Teaching-Professor---Biology-Anatomy---Physiology_JR10004605": {"title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Biology Anatomy & Physiology", "description": "Posted: 2025-10-03\nFull time\n\nCurrent Employees: If you are currently employed at any of the Universities of Wisconsin, log in to Workday to apply through the internal application process. Position Title: Assistant Teaching Professor - Biology Anatomy & Physiology Job Category: Academic Staff Employment Type: Terminal (Fixed Term) Job Profile: Teaching Assistant Professor Job Duties: The Department of Biology in the College of Science and Health at the University of Wisconsin La Crosse (UWL) invites applications for an academic year, non-tenure-track assistant teaching professor position specializing in anatomy and physiology. This is a renewable non-tenure track instructional position. Our colleague will teach in our two-semester anatomy and physiology lab series. Depending on expertise and department need, this individual may also teach anatomy and physiology lectures and/or other undergraduate courses in our curriculum, like General Biology, Genetics, or Cell Biology. We seek an engaging teacher with a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring.\u00a0 Potential t o begin either January 2026 or August 2026. A person in a teaching professor position is responsible for teaching undergraduate courses and advising students. In addition to preparing for and holding classes, teaching involves maintaining currency in the content area related to the teaching assignment, evaluating students\u2019 work, assessing student outcomes, maintaining appropriate records, and holding office hours. This individual will provide service to the department, college, and/or university and is encouraged to engage in service to the community and/or the profession. Other duties may be assigned by the chair or dean. The College of Science & Health (CSH) at the University of Wisconsin\u2013La Crosse is the university\u2019s largest college, educating more than half of all undergraduates through programs in the natural, physical, computational, mathematical, and health sciences. Instructional Academic Staff play an essential role in delivering high-quality, student-centered teaching that emphasizes applied learning, critical thinking, and community engagement. Faculty and staff teach and mentor students in modern facilities such as the Prairie Springs Science Center and the Health Science Center, which provide state-of-the-art instructional labs, specialized research spaces, and opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration. With a strong tradition of innovative curriculum, hands-on laboratory and field experiences, and undergraduate research, CSH fosters student success across disciplines, as reflected in high job placement and graduate/professional school continuation rates. Instructional Academic Staff appointments directly support this mission, making a meaningful and lasting impact on student learning and achievement. The review of applications starts on October 31, 2025 . Applications received on or before October 31st \u00a0are prioritized and review will continue until the position(s) is/are filled. Initial interviews will be conducted virtually,\u00a0with shortlisted candidates invited to campus. Key Job Responsibilities: Collaborates with department faculty and staff to develop teaching strategies relevant to the discipline Develops and designs curriculum and instructional material relevant to a course of instruction Contributes to the development of teaching and learning scholarly work including publications and presentations Contributes to the strategic development of curriculum and academic content through various mediums to ensure the integrity of the educational mission of the work unit Advises students on academic and career direction within a specific field of study Facilitates classroom, online and/or laboratory instruction, including assessment of student performance May supervise student employees involved in development or delivery of instruction Department: Biology Required Qualifications: Master\u2019s degree in biology, or a closely related field.\u00a0 Ability to teach courses in anatomy and physiology Preferred Qualifications: One or more of the following:\u00a0 \u00a0 PhD Prior university teaching experience Experience teaching anatomy and physiology How to Apply: Required application documents CV Cover Letter References Contact Information Contact Information: Christine Schwartz cschwartz@uwlax.edu Special Notes: Application deadlines \u00a0 TO ENSURE CONSIDERATION: Priority consideration is given to those candidates who apply by the listed \u2018First Review Date\u2019. Applications received after that date may be considered at the discretion of the search committee. Application materials will be evaluated, and the most qualified applicants will be invited to participate in the next step of the selection process. Incomplete and/or late application materials may not receive consideration. If you have questions regarding this recruitment, or if you are not able to complete the application online due to a disability or system problem, please contact the Office of Human Resources.\u00a0 Confidentiality of Applicant Materials \u00a0 UWL is a state agency and subject to Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records Law. UWL will not, however, reveal the identities of applicants who request confidentiality in writing except as may be required by Wisconsin\u2019s Open Records law. In certain circumstances, the identities of \u201cfinal candidates\u201d and/or the identity of the appointed applicant must be revealed upon request.\u00a0 \u00a0 CBC & Reference Check Policy \u00a0 All candidates for employment are subject to a pre-employment screening which includes a criminal background check, work authorization, and verification of education. It will also require you and your references to answer questions regarding sexual violence and sexual harassment.\u00a0 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (Clery Act) \u00a0 For the UWL Annual Security and Fire Safety Reports (i.e., Clery Report), which includes statistics about reported crimes and information about campus security policies, see http://www.uwlax.edu/student-life/student-resources/annual-security-report/ or contact the University Police Department at 608.785.9000.\u00a0 INFORMATION\u202fABOUT\u202fYOUR\u202fBENEFITS\u00a0 Your benefits add an additional 40%+ to the overall financial package from the university.\u00a0 Highlights include:\u00a0 paid vacation for 12-month positions.\u00a0 excellent flexible health insurance with low co-pays and good coverage.\u00a0 paid holidays and sick days after 5 years of employment, you become vested in our retirement system which ensures income post-career.\u00a0 benefits at\u202fUWL\u202fare highly competitive with local industry and some of the strongest in state and nation.\u00a0 \u00a0 Benefit eligibility is determined at the point of hire. This information is provided for illustrative purposes only. Benefits are also pro-rated based on the appointment percentage. UW is an Equal Opportunity Employer Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, pregnancy, disability, status as a protected veteran, or any other bases protected by applicable federal or State law and UW System policies. We are committed to building a workforce that represents a variety of backgrounds, perspectives, and skills, and encourage all qualified individuals to apply."}}, "rows": {"https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Biology_JR10015507": {"school_id": 1541, "posting_url": "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Biology_JR10015507", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor in Science Education/Biology", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Biology", "area_key_words": "Science Education/Biology", "deadline_of_application": "November 2, 2026", "posted_date": "2026-10-15", "position_start_date": "8/23/2027"}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Teaching-Professor---Exercise-Sports-Science_JR10014672": {"school_id": 1541, "posting_url": "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Teaching-Professor---Exercise-Sports-Science_JR10014672", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Exercise Sports Science", "position_type": "Lecturer", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Exercise & Sport Science", "area_key_words": "Exercise Sports Science; Assistant Professor Job Duties", "deadline_of_application": "November 16, 2026", "posted_date": "2026-10-13", "position_start_date": "August 23, 2027"}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Data-Science_JR10015740": {"school_id": 1541, "posting_url": "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Data-Science_JR10015740", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor - Data Science", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Mathematics & Statistics", "area_key_words": "Data Science; statistics", "deadline_of_application": "November 6, 2026", "posted_date": "2026-10-09", "position_start_date": "8/23/2027"}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Mathematics---Statistics_JR10015310": {"school_id": 1541, "posting_url": "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Mathematics---Statistics_JR10015310", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor - Mathematics & Statistics", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Department of Mathematics & Statistics", "area_key_words": "Mathematics & Statistics; scholarly research activities", "deadline_of_application": "October 26, 2026", "posted_date": "2026-10-08", "position_start_date": "8/23/2027"}, "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Economics-NOTICE-OF-FILING_JR10015684": {"school_id": 1541, "posting_url": "https://wisconsin.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/UW_Comprehensives/job/La-Crosse-WI/Assistant-Professor---Economics-NOTICE-OF-FILING_JR10015684", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant 